  {
    "test_name": "Boolean Pre-Validation::singleShapeParityWithBooleanValid",
    "bridge_function": "OCCTShapeBooleanCheckSingle",
    "bridge_output": {
      "type": "value",
      "data": {
        "box": {
          "valid": true,
          "analyzerValid": true
        },
        "sphere": {
          "valid": true,
          "analyzerValid": true
        },
        "thinBox": {
          "valid": false,
          "analyzerValid": false,
          "validWithoutSmallEdgeTest": true
        },
        "overlappingCompound": {
          "valid": false,
          "analyzerValid": false,
          "validWithoutSelfInterferenceTest": true
        }
      }
    },
    "kernel_output": {
      "type": "value",
      "data": {
        "box": {
          "valid": true,
          "analyzerValid": true
        },
        "sphere": {
          "valid": true,
          "analyzerValid": true
        },
        "thinBox": {
          "valid": false,
          "analyzerValid": false,
          "validWithoutSmallEdgeTest": true
        },
        "overlappingCompound": {
          "valid": false,
          "analyzerValid": false,
          "validWithoutSelfInterferenceTest": true
        }
      }
    },
    "comparison": {
      "equal": true,
      "differences": []
    },
    "status": "PASS",
    "source": "Same quantity on both sides, per shape: `valid`, whether the shape is valid for a boolean at the defaults (small-edge and self-interference tests on), and `analyzerValid`, the kernel's own BOPAlgo_ArgumentAnalyzer verdict on the same shape with every mode on, paired with a valid 5 mm sphere as the second argument. Shapes: a centred 10x20x30 box and a 5 mm sphere (valid), a box 10x10x5e-7 (its short edges trip only the small-edge test) and a compound of two overlapping 10 mm cubes at (0,0,0) and (5,5,5) (trips only the self-interference test); each of the last two also carries the check with that one test turned off (`validWithoutSmallEdgeTest`, `validWithoutSelfInterferenceTest`), which is true. The earlier record held [isValidForBoolean, isBooleanValid()] on the bridge side against one flag on the kernel side, both for a box and a sphere for which every setting of both tests answers true, so no drift in the forwarded defaults could show. Bridge: Shape.isValidForBoolean (OCCTShapeBooleanCheckSingle), Shape.analyzeBoolean(_, sphere, operation: .fuse) (OCCTBOPAlgoAnalyzeArguments) and Shape.isBooleanValid with one test off. Kernel: BRepAlgoAPI_Check(s, true, true).IsValid(), BOPAlgo_ArgumentAnalyzer with SetShape1/SetShape2, OperationType FUSE, ArgumentTypeMode/SelfInterMode/SmallEdgeMode true, Perform, !HasFaulty, and BRepAlgoAPI_Check with one test off; the singleShapeParityWithBooleanValid lines of the transcript.",
    "probe": "Scripts/repro/766-modeling-boolean-check/probe-evidence-fix.mm (transcript-evidence-fix.txt)"
  },
