    "status": "PASS",
    "source": "Same quantity on both sides, per pair: `valid`, whether the two shapes are valid for a boolean together at the defaults (operation unknown, small-edge and self-interference tests on), and `analyzerValid`, the kernel's own BOPAlgo_ArgumentAnalyzer verdict on the pair (operation FUSE, every mode on). Pairs: box and sphere (valid), the thin box and the sphere (small-edge fault; `validWithoutSmallEdgeTest` is the same check with that test off), the box and the overlapping compound (self-interference fault in the second argument; `validWithoutSelfInterferenceTest`) and the overlapping compound and the sphere. Shapes as in singleShapeParityWithBooleanValid. The earlier record held one flag for a box and a sphere, where isValidForBoolean(with:) and isBooleanValidWith are one call. Bridge: Shape.isValidForBoolean(with:) (OCCTShapeBooleanCheckPair) and Shape.analyzeBoolean(_, _, operation: .fuse) (OCCTBOPAlgoAnalyzeArguments), Shape.isBooleanValidWith with one test off. Kernel: BRepAlgoAPI_Check(a, b, BOPAlgo_UNKNOWN, true, true).IsValid() and BOPAlgo_ArgumentAnalyzer as above; the pairParityWithBooleanValidWith lines of the transcript.",
    "probe": "Scripts/repro/766-modeling-boolean-check/probe-evidence-fix.mm (transcript-evidence-fix.txt)"
  }
